<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cynĭcus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνικός</span> (doglike).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Subst., a Cynic philosopher, a Cynic</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 17, 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 3, 20, 68</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 17, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 13,
				121</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nudi dolia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of Diogenes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 309</span></i>
			.—Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cynĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>Cynic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">institutio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 16, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cena,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 14</span></i>
			; and in * adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cynĭcē</span></b> , <i>after the manner of the Cynics</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Stich. 5, 4, 22</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Suffering by</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπασμὸς κυνικός</span>, <i>spasmodic distortion</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 5,
				24, § 60</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 2,
				2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
